The draft avoids the worst failure modes:

no hype language;
no manifesto voice;
no grand claims about civilization;
no claim that AI cannot do serious mathematics;
no claim that all student AI use is cheating;
no unsupported timelines.

Remaining tone risks:

Some paragraphs still read like expanded scaffold cards.
Several sentences are too short in sequence.
A few writer-facing guardrails remain in public prose, especially in the measurability section.
The draft sometimes names the mechanism before making the reader feel the example.

Sources are used conservatively. The draft cites only verified entries in ../ref.bib.
Citation status:

@Avigad2026: used appropriately for AI-assisted mathematics and mathematical understanding.
@Alon2026: used appropriately for the unit-distance example.
@Schwer2026: used appropriately for mathematical practice/community meaning, but the draft should avoid leaning too much on it without rereading exact claims.
@Commelin2026: used appropriately for community, education, and institutional concerns.
@Klowden2026: used appropriately for education/social response, but exact claims should be checked before making stronger claims.
@Gwern2025: used only at the end for assistant-to-replacement pressure, which is appropriate.

Weak evidence areas:

Feedback-cost map beyond mathematics is mostly internal synthesis. Keep it as the author’s model unless Max Welling or another source is verified.
Conjecture economy currently rests on Avigad/Alon plus internal synthesis. Do not cite MathOverflow until verified.
Measurability distortion should not cite the Leiden Declaration until verified.

The post should not read like a sequence of aphorisms. Avoid paragraphs made from many short declarative sentences of the same shape. Do not turn the scaffold fields into prose one by one.
Each section paragraph should have a small internal arc:

state the object or mechanism;
give the example;
draw the consequence;
hand off to the next section.

The paragraph should feel like one developed thought, not a bullet list with punctuation.

Each paragraph must do at least one of the following:

define a mechanism;
give an example;
state a consequence;
state a limitation;
connect one section to the next.

Delete or rewrite paragraphs that mainly sound polished. Also rewrite paragraphs that sound mechanically assembled from the blueprint.
